            <div xml:id="d24">

                <pb facs="0034" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg27"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8511: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-20T13:00:00+08:00">February 20, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 20—7:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. About 1000 Chinese mill workers rioted at Japanese Toyoda cotton mill outside
                    western district of International Settlement this morning but were checked by
                    police. Subsequently 300 blue jackets from Japanese landing force occupied mill
                    property and remain there at present. Shanghai Municipal police report order has
                    been restored and do not expect further disturbances of serious nature to arise
                    over week end.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
